# Analects Book 19 (子張) — draft, second part: lemmata 20–32 = passages 19.20–19.25 (UNITS_B[0] is lemma 20).
# Token format as the pilot (drafts/analects-01/units.py):
#   tokens separated by " | "; a token is  CHARS[PUNCT][=pinyin][/context gloss[//char gloss//char gloss]]
#   a leading "^" breaks the verse line before the token.
# Punctuation is editorial (the edition has none) and always trails the word before it.
# Pinyin defaults to the glossary's first reading; every polyphone states its reading here, and so does
# every bound compound and every character not yet in the glossary (on every occurrence).
# Passages follow Zhu Xi's chapter breaks (heading: 此篇皆記弟子之言而子夏為多子貢次之…凡二十五章; each ○ checked
# in the commentary file KR1h0015_009.txt): 19.20 = unit 20, 19.21 = 21, 19.22 = 22–23, 19.23 = 24–27,
# 19.24 = 28, 19.25 = 29–32. (The ○ inside the comment after 仲尼焉學, 朝音潮焉於䖍反○公孫朝衞大夫, only parts
# Zhu Xi's sound marks from his gloss; it is not a chapter break.) Each stretch holds at most one chapter (no npas).
# All six passages are Zigong's: four sayings or answers of his own, two answers to men who set him above the
# Master (19.23, 19.25) and one to a man who ran the Master down (19.24).
# Line breaks: the lines of t (one more than the ^ breaks after the first token) equal the lines of l in
# every unit. Speech openers (子貢曰：「) stand on a line of their own when the speech runs to more than one line.
# Quotation marks balance within every unit. Where a speech runs on past one of Zhu Xi's comments the
# continuation is left unquoted, Chinese and English alike (as Books 17–18): 19.23 units 26–27 (Zigong, whose
# 子貢曰：「 opens in unit 25, closed at the end of that unit), 19.25 units 31–32 (Zigong, opened and closed in
# unit 30). Each continuation note says whose words they are.
# Cross-references cite the shipped passage numbers: 紂 Zhou, last king of the Shang (18.1 note); 是以 (5.14);
#   下流 (17.24); 仰之 (9.10); 衞 (7.14); 文王 (9.5), 武王 (8.20); 何常師 against 三人行必有我師焉 (7.21);
#   叔孫, one of the Three Families (3.2); 子服景伯 and 以告 (14.38); 賜 Ci naming himself (5.8); 數 shù (7.16);
#   宗廟 (11.25, 14.20); 百官 (14.43); 夫子 of a lord, not the Master (14.38); 不亦…乎 (1.1); 毁 (15.24);
#   子禽 (1.10), 陳亢 (16.13); 及 'to come up to' (5.20); 階 (10.4); 道 dǎo (12.23 precedent); 如之何 (2.20);
#   邦家 (17.18).
# Repeats and shipped English kept: 子貢 'Zigong'; 君子 'the gentleman'; 夫子 'the Master' (l), 'our Master' in
#   Zigong's mouth (i, as 1.10), 'that lord' of Shusun Wushu (27; 14.38's 'that lord' of Jisun); 賜 'Ci';
#   子服景伯 'Zifu Jingbo' with 以告 'reported it' (25; 14.38); 下 | 流 unbound 'low down the stream' (20; 17.24);
